      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Pero Ranginui y Papatūānuku todavía se amaban.",
          "en": "But Ranginui and Papatūānuku still loved each other."
        },
        {
          "es": "Ranginui lloraba por su esposa. Sus lágrimas caían sobre ella como rocío, de madrugada.",
          "en": "Ranginui wept for his wife. His tears fell on her as dew, in the early morning."
        },
        {
          "es": "Y de Papatūānuku subían nieblas hacia el cielo, como suspiros de añoranza.",
          "en": "And from Papatūānuku, mists rose toward the sky, like sighs of longing."
        },
        {
          "es": "En la versión de Grey, por eso hay rocío al amanecer y niebla que sube de los valles.",
          "en": "In Grey's version, that is why there is dew at dawn, and mist rising from the valleys."
        },
        {
          "es": "¿Tú los habrías separado, sabiendo cuánto iban a sufrir?",
          "en": "Would you have pushed them apart, knowing how much they would grieve?"
        }
